<title>USA: US Labor's Herman to meet with Teamsters, then UPS.</title>
<headline>US Labor's Herman to meet with Teamsters, then UPS.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Labor Department said that separate meetings have been set for Monday afternoon between U.S. Labor Secretary Alexis Herman and United Parcel Service (UPS) officials and striking Teamsters Union leaders.</p>
<p>The department said Herman will meet with Teamsters at 1300 EDT (1700 GMT) and with UPS officials at 1530 EDT (1930 GMT) in an effort to end the eight-day strike that has crippled the nation's largest package carrier.</p>
</text>
